# CarrierOS Product Design

> **Canonical governance:** `/constitution/` (see `INDEX.md`). This rule is a **UI summary**; **folder wins on conflict**. Precedence: Master Constitution v1.0 → Charter → Foundation → Engineering Constitution → AI Safety → this design rule.

> **Canonical design system:** `/docs/design-system/` (start at `docs/design-system/00-README.md`) — permanent Transpo.ai Enterprise Design System. Prefer that folder over this summary for design detail.

CarrierOS is **not a TMS**. It is a premium operations product that should feel like Apple, Linear, and Stripe — calm, confident, and instantly legible.

## Core Principles

- **No clutter** — show only what the user needs right now; hide secondary detail behind progressive disclosure.
- **No unnecessary borders** — use spacing, typography, and subtle background shifts to separate content, not boxes and grid lines.
- **No developer-looking tables** — prefer cards, lists, and scannable rows.
- **No tiny text** — body copy comfortable at a glance.
- **No empty white space** — every screen intentional and complete.
- **Two-second comprehension** — plain language, not jargon or internal codes.
- **One-click tasks** — assign, send rate con, request POD, invoice, notify broker open a single modal or preview.

## Loading · Color · Typography

- Never blank white pages — skeleton loaders on `#F5F7FA`; shimmer; fade-in.
- Semantic colors only: Blue info · Green success · Orange warning · Red critical · Gray inactive.
- Page title Bold · Card titles SemiBold · Labels Medium · Values Regular · Important numbers Bold.

## Interaction · Five-Question Test

Every control does a meaningful action; disable + tooltip when unavailable. Never dead clicks.

1. What is happening? 2. Any problem? 3. What next? 4. Who to contact? 5. One-click finish?

Would this feel at home in Linear or Stripe? If not, simplify. Never at the expense of `/constitution`.
